  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Regaining and Improving access to EiE Ph-1 (MOZ127)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This 5-month project is part of a HPD contingency framework signed with UNICEF. The project aims to help meet the most urgent EiE needs in response to Tropical Cyclone Freddy in two affected provinces: Zambezia (Namacurra and Maganja de Costa districts) and Inhambane (Massinga and Vilankulo).  _x000d_
_x000d_
PD Output 1: Teachers provided with learning/teaching material_x000d_
&#x2022; Provide 100 teachers with teaching kits_x000d_
PD Output 2: Enable access to education and WASH in schools on areas affected by the emergency_x000d_
&#x2022; Construct 20 Temporary Learning Spaces (TLS), including payment of local manpower (CfW): 3 classrooms each TLS_x000d_
&#x2022; Construct 60 gender-sensitive, inclusive latrines (3 x 20TLS)._x000d_
PD Output 3: Girls receive MHM kits accompanied with training/orientation on MHM._x000d_
&#x2022; Distribute 780 MHM kits to adolescent girls_x000d_
PD Output 4: Teachers are equipped with knowledge and skills on cross-sectoral protection issues (GBV, teacher code of conduct, MHPSS, VAC Referrals) and DRR_x000d_
&#x2022; Conduct teachers training on MHPSS, teachers conduct, VAC, GBV and referral and DRR in coordination with District Directorates of Education</narrative>
  </description>
